uses as an end point. All HRs are reported with the 95&#x00025; confidence interval (CI) in parentheses.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote6"><label>b</label><p><italic>P</italic>-values for linear trend were calculated by treating personality subscales as continuous variables.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote7"><label>c</label><p>The total numbers of subjects or deaths from all causes were used in the analyses.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote8"><label>d</label><p>Digestive organs: oesophagus, stomach, small intestine, colon, rectum, and anus.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote9"><label>e</label><p>Respiratory organs: nasal cavity, middle ear, accessory sinuses, larynx, trachea, bronchus, and lung.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>